  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "Angle reasoning is the heart of IGCSE geometry: angles on lines and in polygons, and the family of <strong>circle theorems</strong>. Every answer should be justified with a reason, not just a number.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Polygons",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Interior angles of an \\( n \\)-sided polygon sum to \\( (n-2)\\times 180^{\\circ} \\). The exterior angles always sum to \\( 360^{\\circ} \\), so a regular polygon has each exterior angle \\( \\dfrac{360^{\\circ}}{n} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Circle theorems",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "① The angle at the centre is <em>twice</em> the angle at the circumference on the same arc. ② The angle in a semicircle is \\( 90^{\\circ} \\). ③ Angles in the same segment are equal. ④ Opposite angles of a cyclic quadrilateral sum to \\( 180^{\\circ} \\). ⑤ A tangent meets the radius at \\( 90^{\\circ} \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "The first theorem is the one students doubt most — so watch it directly. Point \\( P \\) slides around the major arc while \\( A \\) and \\( B \\) stay fixed; the inscribed angle never changes, and it is always exactly half the central angle.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "explorer",
        "title": {
          "en": "⊙ Explorer · Inscribed &amp; central angle",
          "ar": null
        },
        "canvasId": "circleCanvas",
        "ariaLabel": {
          "en": "A circle with a fixed chord AB, the central angle at O, and the inscribed angle at a movable point P",
          "ar": null
        },
        "dataPanel": {
          "btnId": "circleDataBtn",
          "panelId": "circleDataPanel",
          "descId": "circleDataDesc",
          "rowsId": "circleDataRows",
          "caption": {
            "en": "Coordinates of the four labelled points on the circle",
            "ar": null
          },
          "columns": [
            {
              "en": "point",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "x",
              "ar": null
            },
            {
              "en": "y",
              "ar": null
            }
          ]
        },
        "controls": [
          {
            "id": "circleP",
            "label": {
              "en": "Slide <b>P</b> around the major arc",
              "ar": null
            },
            "min": 0,
            "max": 100,
            "value": 50,
            "step": 1,
            "ariaLabel": {
              "en": "Slide P around the major arc",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ],
        "readouts": [
          {
            "id": "circleInscribed",
            "label": {
              "en": "inscribed&nbsp; ∠APB",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "indigo",
            "value": "—"
          },
          {
            "id": "circleCentral",
            "label": {
              "en": "central&nbsp; ∠AOB",
              "ar": null
            },
            "colorClass": "amber",
            "value": "—"
          }
        ],
        "note": {
          "en": "Wherever \\(P\\) sits on the arc, \\( \\angle APB=\\tfrac12\\,\\angle AOB \\). The inscribed angle holds steady.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Triangle angle sum",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\alpha+\\beta+\\gamma=180° \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Exterior angle",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Exterior \\( = \\) sum of two non-adjacent interior angles",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Polygon angle sum",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( S=(n-2)\\times180° \\); each interior \\( =\\frac{S}{n} \\) (regular)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Parallel line angles",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "Alternate = equal; co-interior \\( = 180° \\); corresponding = equal",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 5.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Find each interior angle of a regular pentagon.</p><p>Interior sum \\( =(5-2)\\times 180^{\\circ}=540^{\\circ} \\); divide equally among five angles:</p>\\[ \\frac{540^{\\circ}}{5}=108^{\\circ}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 5.B",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Points \\( A \\) and \\( B \\) lie on a circle, centre \\( O \\), with \\( \\angle AOB=80^{\\circ} \\). Find the angle subtended by \\( AB \\) at the circumference.</p><p>By the centre–circumference theorem the inscribed angle is half the central angle:</p>\\[ \\tfrac12\\times 80^{\\circ}=40^{\\circ}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Similarity &amp; Congruence",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<strong>Congruent</strong> shapes are identical in shape and size (SSS, SAS, ASA, RHS). <strong>Similar</strong> shapes have the same angles; corresponding sides are in the same ratio \\(k\\). Area scales as \\(k^2\\); volume scales as \\(k^3\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Congruence",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "SSS, SAS, ASA, RHS",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Similar — lengths",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "ratio \\(k\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Similar — areas",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "ratio \\(k^{2}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Similar — volumes",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "ratio \\(k^{3}\\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 5.C — Similar areas",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Two similar triangles have corresponding sides in the ratio \\(3:5\\). If the smaller triangle has area \\(18\\text{ cm}^2\\), find the area of the larger.</p>\\[\\text{Area ratio}=\\left(\\tfrac{5}{3}\\right)^{\\!2}=\\tfrac{25}{9}.\\qquad A_{\\text{large}}=18\\times\\tfrac{25}{9}=50\\text{ cm}^2.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "def",
        "label": {
          "en": "● Construction &amp; Loci",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "A <strong>locus</strong> is the set of all points satisfying a given condition. Key loci: (1) equidistant from a fixed point → <em>circle</em>; (2) equidistant from two fixed points → <em>perpendicular bisector</em>; (3) equidistant from two lines → <em>angle bisector</em>; (4) fixed distance from a line → <em>pair of parallel lines</em>.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Two similar cylinders have radii 4 cm and 6 cm. If the volume of the smaller is \\(160\\pi\\) cm³, find the volume of the larger.",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "\\(k=6/4=1.5\\). Volume ratio \\(=1.5^3=3.375\\). Volume \\(=160\\pi\\times3.375=540\\pi\\) cm³.",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
